Z||000000||poupas||06-05-2001||07:04 PM||||Can anyone tell me whether the Fiero has the same bolt pattern as a '95 Toyota Camry?   <BR>                Thanks    Andrew<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||06-05-2001||07:17 PM||||Fiero is 5x100 <P>It seems that the Toyota is 5/114.3 from what I'm finding on it...  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||poupas||06-05-2001||08:05 PM||||Thanks for the info. I had found a set of 17 inch rims with rubber for pretty cheap, I knew they were 5 lug, and from a Toyota, but didnt know if they matched. Too bad.||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||06-05-2001||09:33 PM||||If you do a search for rims or wheels, you will get some great info on what rims will fit our cars.  I used this list when I went to the yard and got a great set of Beretta GT 16" rims.  I knew they would fit, but there are several on the list I would not have figured.<P>Rob <P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||12
Z||000004||grizco||06-06-2001||01:10 AM||||Here's a link to that list. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004113.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004113.html</A> <BR>Looks like only the 86-91 Camry rims fit.<BR>If their aftermarket wheels there might be a chance that the mounting holes are slotted so that they can be used on multiple cars with bolt patterns that are close.<P>josh||||reg||1
